1
00:00:00,123 --> 00:00:01,123
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

2
00:00:01,123 --> 00:00:02,123
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

3
00:00:02,123 --> 00:00:03,690
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

4
00:00:03,690 --> 00:00:06,890
[Episode 9]

5
00:00:20,724 --> 00:00:22,424
You startled me!

6
00:00:24,579 --> 00:00:27,623
- What are you doing?
- Huh? What is it?

7
00:00:28,339 --> 00:00:33,190
I feel like I said something important
and heard something even more important.

8
00:00:35,007 --> 00:00:38,456
Wow, I never knew there was
honey tea in the break room.

9
00:00:40,058 --> 00:00:43,007
You don't usually drink like that.

10
00:00:43,007 --> 00:00:45,412
You should've gone home
and become one with your bed.

11
00:00:45,412 --> 00:00:47,026
Why'd you come in on the weekend?

12
00:00:47,026 --> 00:00:50,211
Why did you come in, then?

13
00:00:50,211 --> 00:00:55,190
Me? Are you asking me?
Are you genuinely curious?

14
00:00:56,014 --> 00:01:00,456
Then shall I give you a sincere answer?

15
00:01:01,159 --> 00:01:03,190
"Look into the unusual death
in Hyeonsa-dong."

16
00:01:03,190 --> 00:01:06,390
"Pull a list of the punks recently released
who didn't serve enough time."

17
00:01:06,390 --> 00:01:08,099
You're making my head spin.

18
00:01:08,099 --> 00:01:11,811
My head's already not exactly
in working order.

19
00:01:11,811 --> 00:01:14,943
[Violent Crimes Team 2]
And that's not all. See this?

20
00:01:14,943 --> 00:01:17,423
Endless Kingfisher material?

21
00:01:17,423 --> 00:01:18,645
This is why I'm...

22
00:01:18,645 --> 00:01:21,123
Need to take the exam again?

23
00:01:24,711 --> 00:01:27,745
[Kingfisher Case Files]
Let's see. Today...

24
00:01:27,745 --> 00:01:29,091
[Haegong-dong Gosiwon Case]
Oh, Haegong-dong Gosiwon?

25
00:01:29,091 --> 00:01:30,327
Oh, this is that case.

26
00:01:30,327 --> 00:01:32,915
Kingfisher's last case before disappearing.

27
00:01:34,023 --> 00:01:36,390
I think I'm finally getting somewhere.

28
00:01:39,616 --> 00:01:41,535
[Haegong-dong Case Overview]

29
00:01:42,545 --> 00:01:44,738
[With seven-year-old Yeon Cheol present]
Huh? What's this?

30
00:01:44,738 --> 00:01:47,574
There was a seven-year-old child
at the scene?

31
00:01:47,574 --> 00:01:51,403
But there's a side of him people don't know.

32
00:01:51,403 --> 00:01:54,603
A punk who shot a dad dead

33
00:01:54,603 --> 00:01:58,219
right in front of his seven-year-old son.

34
00:01:58,219 --> 00:01:59,915
<i>Actually, I know.</i>

35
00:01:59,915 --> 00:02:03,323
I'm telling you, I saw Kingfisher.

36
00:02:04,390 --> 00:02:09,875
I was there at the Haegong-dong
Gosiwon case that day.

37
00:02:09,875 --> 00:02:12,190
- Ah!
- Oh, you startled me!

38
00:02:14,589 --> 00:02:18,079
Bo Na, you didn't answer,
so I left a message.

39
00:02:18,079 --> 00:02:19,893
<i>Did you just see it?</i>

40
00:02:19,893 --> 00:02:21,389
You pulled another prank on me?

41
00:02:21,389 --> 00:02:23,190
Oh, jeez.

42
00:02:23,190 --> 00:02:26,779
I figured you'd be home
since it's the weekend.

43
00:02:26,779 --> 00:02:29,207
Was I being rude?

44
00:02:29,207 --> 00:02:31,435
Should I wait out here?

45
00:02:31,435 --> 00:02:34,656
You can wait inside if you don't mind.

46
00:02:36,356 --> 00:02:37,390
[Bo Na]

47
00:02:37,390 --> 00:02:38,471
[Speakerphone]

48
00:02:38,471 --> 00:02:41,390
Bo Na, is it okay if I do that?

49
00:02:43,123 --> 00:02:45,399
Listen carefully.

50
00:02:45,399 --> 00:02:47,612
<i>If you say even one useless word,</i>

51
00:02:47,612 --> 00:02:50,527
you'll die by my hand.

52
00:02:50,527 --> 00:02:53,427
That's hurtful. You don't trust me?

53
00:02:53,427 --> 00:02:58,233
Back then and now, ever since "that day."

54
00:02:58,233 --> 00:03:02,255
If you don't want to die,
you'd better remember what I said.

55
00:03:02,255 --> 00:03:04,823
Thanks for welcoming me, Bo Na.

56
00:03:05,583 --> 00:03:08,390
Come quickly. I miss you.

57
00:03:11,467 --> 00:03:13,167
Please come on in.

58
00:03:21,245 --> 00:03:24,323
Congratulations. You're pregnant.

59
00:03:24,323 --> 00:03:26,263
You're five weeks along.

60
00:03:26,263 --> 00:03:27,263
[Four Years Ago, "That Day"]

61
00:03:27,263 --> 00:03:30,151
Right here, do you see this little bean?

62
00:03:30,151 --> 00:03:31,563
That's the gestational sac.

63
00:03:31,563 --> 00:03:33,027
The gestational sac?

64
00:03:33,027 --> 00:03:35,256
Yeah.

65
00:03:35,256 --> 00:03:36,915
[Prenatal Care Booklet]

66
00:03:36,915 --> 00:03:39,743
<i>You're still in the early stages,
so you need to be extra careful, okay?</i>

67
00:03:39,743 --> 00:03:43,683
<i>Avoid running, strenuous exercise,
and lifting heavy objects.</i>

68
00:03:43,683 --> 00:03:45,435
<i>It's also best to avoid
rushing up and down stairs</i>

69
00:03:45,435 --> 00:03:50,167
or making sudden movements
like sitting down and standing up quickly.

70
00:03:50,167 --> 00:03:53,967
Most importantly, try to stay relaxed.

71
00:03:53,967 --> 00:03:57,223
Stress can have a negative effect.

72
00:04:01,156 --> 00:04:03,190
[Calls]

73
00:04:03,190 --> 00:04:05,256
[My Santa]

74
00:04:08,556 --> 00:04:10,690
[Incoming Call, My Santa]

75
00:04:10,690 --> 00:04:12,790
[My Santa]

76
00:04:14,195 --> 00:04:15,195
Tae Seong.

77
00:04:15,195 --> 00:04:17,283
<i>Yeah, honey. Did you have lunch?</i>

78
00:04:17,283 --> 00:04:19,103
Of course. Look at the time. I ate ages ago.

79
00:04:19,103 --> 00:04:20,163
What about you, Tae Seong?

80
00:04:20,163 --> 00:04:21,959
<i>I'm on my way to get something to eat.</i>

81
00:04:21,959 --> 00:04:24,551
<i>I just finished an interview.</i>

82
00:04:24,551 --> 00:04:26,099
You must be starving.

83
00:04:26,099 --> 00:04:28,056
<i>What's wrong with your voice?</i>

84
00:04:28,802 --> 00:04:30,502
<i>Are you sick?</i>

85
00:04:31,987 --> 00:04:35,056
No, I'm perfectly fine. Why do you ask?

86
00:04:37,117 --> 00:04:38,935
Are you going to be late today?

87
00:04:38,935 --> 00:04:42,567
<i>Even if I leave right after lunch,</i>

88
00:04:42,567 --> 00:04:44,107
<i>I'll probably have to stop by the office,</i>

89
00:04:44,107 --> 00:04:46,555
<i>so it'll be evening by the time I get there.</i>

90
00:04:46,555 --> 00:04:48,347
I wish you could come early.

91
00:04:48,347 --> 00:04:50,079
[Prenatal Care Booklet]
So we can have dinner together.

92
00:04:50,079 --> 00:04:52,455
I have something to show you.

93
00:04:52,455 --> 00:04:56,623
<i>Of course, I'll come early.
I'll wrap things up and fly home.</i>

94
00:05:07,331 --> 00:05:09,954
Have you figured out
what you're going to do next?

95
00:05:09,954 --> 00:05:10,954
Not really.

96
00:05:10,954 --> 00:05:14,635
I was thinking of opening
a little shop with my severance pay,

97
00:05:14,635 --> 00:05:16,583
but I don't have anything specific in mind.

98
00:05:16,583 --> 00:05:18,539
If I had my way,

99
00:05:18,539 --> 00:05:22,671
I'd like to spend the rest of my life
looking at beautiful things.

100
00:05:22,671 --> 00:05:25,890
Then you should open a flower shop.
Flowers are beautiful.

101
00:05:27,599 --> 00:05:30,263
Hey, wow!

102
00:05:30,263 --> 00:05:34,995
Even Yoo Bo Na knows flowers are pretty.
Feels like a whole different era.

103
00:05:34,995 --> 00:05:38,387
Well, I guess the world has changed.

104
00:05:38,387 --> 00:05:40,547
Your world has.

105
00:05:40,547 --> 00:05:43,423
Well, you look so much brighter too.

106
00:05:43,423 --> 00:05:45,656
I guess married life
is treating you well, huh?

107
00:05:55,359 --> 00:06:00,356
But once the baby arrives,
does the world really change?

108
00:06:05,491 --> 00:06:07,423
Are you planning to have a baby?

109
00:06:10,231 --> 00:06:12,363
I can't quite explain how I feel.

110
00:06:12,363 --> 00:06:14,287
It scares me too.

111
00:06:14,287 --> 00:06:19,451
The word "mom" just feels
so far away from me.

112
00:06:19,451 --> 00:06:21,215
You're worrying about nothing.

113
00:06:21,215 --> 00:06:23,087
You'll still be you after you become a mom.

114
00:06:23,087 --> 00:06:26,295
"Your world won't change.
It just gets bigger."

115
00:06:26,295 --> 00:06:29,190
That's what my grandma always used to say.

116
00:06:30,015 --> 00:06:32,323
And that's what I believed too.

117
00:06:34,651 --> 00:06:36,771
Do you think I can really do this?

118
00:06:36,771 --> 00:06:38,823
You're already doing a great job.

119
00:06:39,891 --> 00:06:44,856
You've got herbal tea in front of you
instead of your beloved coffee.

120
00:06:48,479 --> 00:06:50,083
Don't worry.

121
00:06:50,083 --> 00:06:52,803
Your world has already changed once.

122
00:06:52,803 --> 00:06:57,623
It's only going to get bigger
and stronger from now on.

123
00:07:13,347 --> 00:07:14,899
- Yes, Team Leader.
- <i>Oh, Director Yoo.</i>

124
00:07:14,899 --> 00:07:18,111
The Yeon Chang Bok meeting today
has fallen through.

125
00:07:18,111 --> 00:07:19,790
Ugh, that darn punk...

126
00:07:19,790 --> 00:07:23,423
He made a move
before Manager Go could do anything.

127
00:07:23,423 --> 00:07:24,699
Yeah.

128
00:07:24,699 --> 00:07:28,023
I'm chasing him right now.
He's getting away in a taxi.

129
00:07:28,023 --> 00:07:29,543
He moved faster than we expected.

130
00:07:29,543 --> 00:07:34,603
Who knew he'd change his mind
the second he got to the hospital?

131
00:07:34,603 --> 00:07:36,856
If we lose him now,

132
00:07:36,856 --> 00:07:40,779
I don't think we'll get
another chance to catch him easily.

133
00:07:40,779 --> 00:07:44,056
We need to revise the scenario. I'll go.

134
00:07:44,056 --> 00:07:46,256
Keep me updated on his route.

135
00:08:54,723 --> 00:08:56,056
What did you bring?

136
00:08:56,056 --> 00:08:57,488
Forget that. The money!

137
00:08:57,488 --> 00:08:59,188
Here.

138
00:09:10,615 --> 00:09:11,823
- Team Leader.
- Yeah?

139
00:09:11,823 --> 00:09:14,083
[Haegong-dong Gosiwon]
Yeon Chang Bok's mom and son are here.

140
00:09:14,083 --> 00:09:15,223
A son?

141
00:09:15,223 --> 00:09:18,239
The newborn his mom was holding
when he was arrested.

142
00:09:18,239 --> 00:09:21,063
Yeah, I'll wait until they leave.

143
00:09:21,063 --> 00:09:23,043
The police are about to storm in.

144
00:09:23,043 --> 00:09:24,295
<i>This doesn't look good.</i>

145
00:09:24,295 --> 00:09:26,251
Not in front of the kid.

146
00:09:26,251 --> 00:09:27,951
I'll just wait.

147
00:09:30,436 --> 00:09:31,955
Surprise!

148
00:09:31,955 --> 00:09:34,256
Hi, my friend.

149
00:09:50,539 --> 00:09:52,103
- It came out again.
- Right?

150
00:09:52,103 --> 00:09:53,627
Isn't it awesome?

151
00:09:53,627 --> 00:09:55,883
- Another one!
- There it is again.

152
00:09:55,883 --> 00:09:57,819
Honey, you're back?

153
00:09:57,819 --> 00:09:58,819
Mommy!

154
00:09:58,819 --> 00:10:01,419
More and more toys
keep coming out of the doll.

155
00:10:01,419 --> 00:10:02,619
Yeah?

156
00:10:02,619 --> 00:10:06,123
Sergei brought another gift for Yul.

157
00:10:07,079 --> 00:10:08,647
You should've told me you were coming.

158
00:10:08,647 --> 00:10:10,523
Surprise!

159
00:10:11,967 --> 00:10:13,823
Hi, my friend.

160
00:10:15,107 --> 00:10:16,719
It's here, it's here!

161
00:10:16,719 --> 00:10:19,256
- What's here?
- Chicken! Chicken's here!

162
00:10:19,256 --> 00:10:23,331
I think your husband's jealous of us.

163
00:10:23,331 --> 00:10:26,290
Behave yourself.

164
00:10:27,390 --> 00:10:29,499
[Tae Seong Chicken]
I didn't have anything proper to serve him,

165
00:10:29,499 --> 00:10:31,987
so I asked Sun Il for a favor.

166
00:10:31,987 --> 00:10:34,603
I could've just taken him out for dinner.

167
00:10:34,603 --> 00:10:37,190
You're not feeling well.
Why go through all that trouble?

168
00:10:37,190 --> 00:10:41,790
No, I'm fine. I told you I wanted
to see your Russian friend too.

169
00:10:43,859 --> 00:10:46,291
I didn't know he was that kind of man.

170
00:10:46,291 --> 00:10:48,219
Didn't I tell you he was a man?

171
00:10:48,219 --> 00:10:49,875
I think I did.

172
00:10:49,875 --> 00:10:52,123
Yeah, you said he was a man.

173
00:10:52,856 --> 00:10:56,127
You just didn't say he was that good-looking.

174
00:10:56,127 --> 00:10:58,259
- Huh?
- What?

175
00:10:58,259 --> 00:10:59,843
You think he's a good-looking man?

176
00:10:59,843 --> 00:11:01,103
He's pretty handsome.

177
00:11:01,103 --> 00:11:03,023
You, seriously...

178
00:11:04,491 --> 00:11:06,546
Let's go eat too.

179
00:11:11,367 --> 00:11:14,243
Korean fried chicken really is the best.

180
00:11:14,243 --> 00:11:15,599
It's so good.

181
00:11:15,599 --> 00:11:18,223
I'm glad it suits your taste.

182
00:11:18,223 --> 00:11:20,691
But Sergei...

183
00:11:20,691 --> 00:11:24,139
Just call me Seul Gi. That's easier.

184
00:11:24,139 --> 00:11:25,267
I'm good with that too.

185
00:11:25,267 --> 00:11:27,223
Oh, alright.

186
00:11:28,791 --> 00:11:33,135
Seul Gi, I heard you were born in Russia.

187
00:11:33,135 --> 00:11:34,783
But your Korean is really good.

188
00:11:34,783 --> 00:11:38,367
My mama is Korean.

189
00:11:38,367 --> 00:11:42,456
And I got used to the language
from playing with Bo Na since we were kids.

190
00:11:45,955 --> 00:11:48,791
Yeah, we lived in the same
neighborhood back then.

191
00:11:48,791 --> 00:11:52,619
I think I first met Bo Na when we were eight.

192
00:11:52,619 --> 00:11:55,615
Right after you moved to Russia, remember?

193
00:11:55,615 --> 00:11:57,307
You're right.

194
00:11:57,307 --> 00:12:00,090
So you've known each other for a long time.

195
00:12:00,847 --> 00:12:03,111
We have.

196
00:12:03,111 --> 00:12:05,639
By the way, are you okay, honey?

197
00:12:05,639 --> 00:12:09,090
Well, he came home so wasted
last night that he blacked out.

198
00:12:09,090 --> 00:12:10,123
- You must be exhausted.
- No...

199
00:12:10,123 --> 00:12:12,343
- Can you really eat this right now?
- No, I'm fine. I'm really fine.

200
00:12:12,343 --> 00:12:16,019
I just enjoy hearing about your past.

201
00:12:16,019 --> 00:12:17,299
- It's good.
- I'm fine.

202
00:12:17,299 --> 00:12:18,719
Well, it's...

203
00:12:18,719 --> 00:12:20,443
When I first met Bo Na,

204
00:12:20,443 --> 00:12:26,111
I said in Korean, "Hi, I'm Sergei."

205
00:12:26,111 --> 00:12:27,767
And she goes, "Seul Gi?"

206
00:12:27,767 --> 00:12:30,251
"No, Sergei."

207
00:12:30,251 --> 00:12:33,623
"Ah! No Seul Gi?"

208
00:12:38,947 --> 00:12:44,199
From that day on,
I was just "No Seul Gi" to Bo Na.

209
00:12:44,199 --> 00:12:46,456
So that's the story behind your nickname.

210
00:12:46,456 --> 00:12:49,987
Yul, chew this slowly and thoroughly, okay?

211
00:12:49,987 --> 00:12:51,647
Mommy, you eat some too.

212
00:12:51,647 --> 00:12:53,456
Is this for me?

213
00:12:54,423 --> 00:12:55,907
It's good. Thank you.

214
00:12:55,907 --> 00:12:58,011
Bo Na, are you eating chicken?

215
00:12:58,011 --> 00:12:59,851
You never used to like chicken.

216
00:12:59,851 --> 00:13:00,971
I do now.

217
00:13:00,971 --> 00:13:03,615
Really? That's interesting.

218
00:13:03,615 --> 00:13:06,095
You used to hate the smell of chicken...

219
00:13:06,095 --> 00:13:08,243
Oh, chicken porridge!

220
00:13:08,243 --> 00:13:10,456
You didn't like chicken porridge either.

221
00:13:11,823 --> 00:13:13,767
- Huh?
- Back then, I did.

222
00:13:13,767 --> 00:13:18,390
It seems there are still a lot of things
you don't know about Bo Na.

223
00:13:19,679 --> 00:13:22,156
Or does she just not tell you
much about herself?

224
00:13:25,179 --> 00:13:29,556
When Bo Na was in school,
some mean kids used to play pranks on her.

225
00:13:29,556 --> 00:13:33,563
They'd secretly dunk
her chicken in muddy water,

226
00:13:33,563 --> 00:13:37,487
or pour strong whiskey into her chicken soup.

227
00:13:37,487 --> 00:13:39,756
So sometimes...

228
00:13:40,611 --> 00:13:43,090
things got physical.

229
00:13:44,563 --> 00:13:47,527
Bo Na was pretty tough back then.

230
00:13:47,527 --> 00:13:49,690
Hey, you don't need to bring that up.

231
00:13:49,690 --> 00:13:55,235
In Korean, we'd say "no mercy."

232
00:13:55,235 --> 00:13:58,551
Bo Na is very self-assured
and clear about what she wants in everything.

233
00:13:58,551 --> 00:14:00,756
She knows exactly what's right and wrong.

234
00:14:01,863 --> 00:14:03,343
- Is that so?
- Yeah.

235
00:14:03,343 --> 00:14:06,575
And Bo Na eats chicken just fine now.
She even likes chicken porridge.

236
00:14:06,575 --> 00:14:09,356
Food tastes different depending on

237
00:14:09,356 --> 00:14:14,271
who you eat it with
and what memories it holds, right?

238
00:14:14,271 --> 00:14:16,395
Oh, I see.

239
00:14:16,395 --> 00:14:18,747
I may not have known
the Bo Na from childhood,

240
00:14:18,747 --> 00:14:20,967
but I know who she is now.

241
00:14:20,967 --> 00:14:25,151
Because what matters
is the present, not the past.

242
00:14:25,151 --> 00:14:26,851
Isn't it?

243
00:14:27,967 --> 00:14:32,099
I was curious what kind of man
Bo Na would end up with.

244
00:14:32,099 --> 00:14:33,911
Looks like she found a good one.

245
00:14:33,911 --> 00:14:37,623
Oh, no. I'm the one who got lucky enough
to meet an amazing woman.

246
00:14:41,567 --> 00:14:42,990
He is so tired now.

247
00:14:42,990 --> 00:14:46,791
Let's finish up and go have some tea, okay?

248
00:14:46,791 --> 00:14:48,491
Alright.

249
00:14:56,007 --> 00:14:57,471
We'll just have tea and come right back.

250
00:14:57,471 --> 00:14:59,495
I'll be back soon, Yul, okay?

251
00:14:59,495 --> 00:15:00,495
Take your time.

252
00:15:00,495 --> 00:15:03,556
You two must have a lot
to catch up on after all this time.

253
00:15:04,703 --> 00:15:07,111
Thanks for the great chicken
and the wonderful conversation.

254
00:15:07,111 --> 00:15:09,566
- Let's catch up again soon.
- Okay.

255
00:15:12,691 --> 00:15:14,711
Goodbye! Little Yul.

256
00:15:14,711 --> 00:15:16,890
Goodbye.

257
00:15:20,435 --> 00:15:22,990
Goodbye, Tae Seong.

258
00:16:04,786 --> 00:16:07,787
Oh, Bo Na, calm down.

259
00:16:07,787 --> 00:16:10,490
I told you not to show your face
in front of me again, didn't I?

260
00:16:11,127 --> 00:16:15,356
Just as I thought,
those two are your Achilles' heels.

261
00:16:16,519 --> 00:16:20,411
Looks like my warning that day
wasn't strong enough.

262
00:16:20,411 --> 00:16:25,923
Having something to protect
is a fatal weakness for killers like us.

263
00:16:33,127 --> 00:16:34,327
Okay.

264
00:16:34,327 --> 00:16:37,207
I'm not coming back.

265
00:16:37,207 --> 00:16:39,123
I promise you.

266
00:16:39,123 --> 00:16:41,747
That's your second warning.

267
00:16:41,747 --> 00:16:43,556
No third chance.

268
00:16:45,271 --> 00:16:46,971
Get lost.

269
00:16:47,939 --> 00:16:50,090
I really meant it.

270
00:16:54,015 --> 00:16:56,956
You seem to have found a good guy.

271
00:17:35,190 --> 00:17:36,556
[Four Years Ago, "That Day"]
No way!

272
00:17:36,556 --> 00:17:39,719
It seems like Yeon Chang Bok escaped
from the hospital while in medical custody.

273
00:17:39,719 --> 00:17:41,799
Yeon Chang Bok?

274
00:17:41,799 --> 00:17:43,690
Yeon Chang Bok...

275
00:17:45,107 --> 00:17:46,621
Oh, that guy...

276
00:17:46,621 --> 00:17:50,183
The aggravated sex offender who broke into
a home and threatened the family?

277
00:17:50,183 --> 00:17:52,006
The lowest of the low.

278
00:17:52,006 --> 00:17:55,055
He pointed the knife at the victim's baby,
not even the victim herself.

279
00:17:55,055 --> 00:17:57,483
The mom eventually
took her own life a few months later.

280
00:17:57,483 --> 00:17:59,939
Right, you covered that case too, didn't you?

281
00:17:59,939 --> 00:18:01,287
Yeah, for a day.

282
00:18:01,287 --> 00:18:06,383
The day Yeon Chang Bok's mom protested
outside the courthouse for leniency.

283
00:18:06,383 --> 00:18:09,435
Yeah, I accompanied the mom
and followed her to her house.

284
00:18:09,435 --> 00:18:11,383
And I even saw Yeon Chang Bok's son.

285
00:18:11,383 --> 00:18:15,056
Someone like that should be
taken out by Kingfisher.

286
00:18:15,767 --> 00:18:17,590
So, are you a Kingfisher fan too, Mr. Nam?

287
00:18:17,590 --> 00:18:21,175
Oh, a lot of reporters secretly
support him, actually.

288
00:18:21,175 --> 00:18:22,715
Hold on.

289
00:18:22,715 --> 00:18:25,556
At this rate, won't Kingfisher
find this punk first?

290
00:18:25,556 --> 00:18:28,990
He's always a step ahead of the cops.

291
00:18:28,990 --> 00:18:32,643
Honestly, that might be better than
getting caught by the police.

292
00:18:32,643 --> 00:18:35,583
Sorry, Mr. Nam, but I think
I should go into the office alone.

293
00:18:35,583 --> 00:18:38,023
What? Why?

294
00:20:41,267 --> 00:20:44,847
Hey, reckless young man.

295
00:20:44,847 --> 00:20:51,647
You need to learn that some doors
in this world should never be opened.

296
00:20:53,619 --> 00:20:55,195
Surprise!

297
00:20:55,195 --> 00:20:57,423
Hi, my friend.

298
00:21:00,991 --> 00:21:02,790
I'll be offline for a bit.

299
00:21:03,559 --> 00:21:04,891
What are you doing here?

300
00:21:04,891 --> 00:21:07,515
Why are you...

301
00:21:07,515 --> 00:21:09,790
How did you know I was here?

302
00:21:17,583 --> 00:21:20,123
Still got those sticky fingers, I see.

303
00:21:21,275 --> 00:21:22,471
What's going on today?

304
00:21:22,471 --> 00:21:25,875
Why are you letting your guard down?
That's not like you.

305
00:21:25,875 --> 00:21:26,879
What brings you to Korea?

306
00:21:26,879 --> 00:21:29,090
I was bored, so I came to visit.

307
00:21:29,090 --> 00:21:31,823
Russia is too boring without you.

308
00:21:31,823 --> 00:21:33,956
Go. I'm working now.

309
00:21:35,651 --> 00:21:38,219
Well, is there a problem?

310
00:21:38,219 --> 00:21:41,423
The client has a visitor, so I'm standing by.

311
00:21:46,239 --> 00:21:48,523
Now that's more like you.

312
00:21:48,523 --> 00:21:52,175
But once the guest leaves, you can do it?

313
00:21:52,175 --> 00:21:53,666
You're still in the very early stages,

314
00:21:53,666 --> 00:21:56,590
so I think you were told to be extra careful.

315
00:21:58,747 --> 00:22:01,090
Where did you even...

316
00:22:01,775 --> 00:22:03,519
Isn't this the time

317
00:22:03,519 --> 00:22:06,723
when you should be focusing on
nothing but beautiful things?

318
00:22:08,139 --> 00:22:13,423
But if you absolutely have to do it,
how about hiring a mercenary?

319
00:22:19,595 --> 00:22:21,435
A mercenary?

320
00:22:21,435 --> 00:22:23,656
The best mercenary.

321
00:22:31,731 --> 00:22:35,123
Then you just pull the trigger.
I'll take care of the rest.

322
00:22:35,927 --> 00:22:37,887
Wise choice.

323
00:22:37,887 --> 00:22:40,695
Not yet, wait.

324
00:22:40,695 --> 00:22:43,456
I need to confirm the location first.

325
00:22:55,387 --> 00:22:58,256
Is there just one guest?

326
00:23:00,347 --> 00:23:02,047
Oh.

327
00:23:02,683 --> 00:23:04,383
A young boy?

328
00:23:04,383 --> 00:23:05,559
His son.

329
00:23:05,559 --> 00:23:09,156
Once the child has left, then...

330
00:23:09,156 --> 00:23:10,290
Target is down.

331
00:23:10,290 --> 00:23:12,356
What on earth are you doing?

332
00:23:19,323 --> 00:23:22,423
Calm down, Bo Na.

333
00:23:22,423 --> 00:23:25,719
You crazy punk! You want to die?

334
00:23:25,719 --> 00:23:30,590
The person holding the gun decides
when to pull the trigger.

335
00:23:30,590 --> 00:23:33,771
- You know that.
- The boy is innocent.

336
00:23:33,771 --> 00:23:35,299
He's done nothing wrong.

337
00:23:35,299 --> 00:23:41,147
"Your name, in death,
only ends up on your tombstone."

338
00:23:41,147 --> 00:23:47,407
"But your sins, even in death,
are passed down to your children."

339
00:23:47,407 --> 00:23:49,423
That's what Mama always used to say.

340
00:23:49,423 --> 00:23:51,156
Shut up!

341
00:23:59,575 --> 00:24:02,163
Did I kill a kid like someone else did?

342
00:24:02,163 --> 00:24:04,235
I didn't, right?

343
00:24:04,235 --> 00:24:05,767
So isn't that enough?

344
00:24:05,767 --> 00:24:08,963
Oh, calm down, Bo Na.

345
00:24:08,963 --> 00:24:11,956
The doctor said stress
isn't good for the baby...

346
00:24:44,556 --> 00:24:45,856
[Not Today, Kwon Tae Seong]

347
00:24:45,856 --> 00:24:48,290
Kwon Tae Seong?

348
00:24:49,419 --> 00:24:51,119
So he's a reporter?

349
00:24:52,691 --> 00:24:54,391
And what's this?

350
00:24:58,767 --> 00:25:00,723
Interesting.

351
00:25:28,511 --> 00:25:30,211
You're awake.

352
00:25:31,963 --> 00:25:34,335
Reporter Kwon Tae Seong.

353
00:25:34,335 --> 00:25:39,156
Forget everything that happened today.

354
00:25:39,899 --> 00:25:44,656
And from now on, you'd better
stop looking into Kingfisher.

355
00:25:46,887 --> 00:25:49,290
If you break your promise,

356
00:25:50,543 --> 00:25:54,083
your wife and your child,

357
00:25:54,083 --> 00:25:56,823
your family could be in danger.

358
00:26:02,711 --> 00:26:04,223
Calm down.

359
00:26:04,223 --> 00:26:07,255
Shh.

360
00:26:07,255 --> 00:26:11,790
As long as you keep your promise,
nothing will happen.

361
00:26:13,243 --> 00:26:15,523
Well, then...

362
00:26:21,155 --> 00:26:23,723
Goodnight, Tae Seong.

363
00:26:29,739 --> 00:26:33,443
Why are you still so angry, Yoo Bo Na?

364
00:26:33,443 --> 00:26:38,403
Did I put a blemish on
Kingfisher's flawless record?

365
00:26:38,403 --> 00:26:43,135
You left a scar on a child that
he'll never forget for the rest of his life.

366
00:26:43,135 --> 00:26:46,375
Did I force you to give up the gun?

367
00:26:46,375 --> 00:26:48,303
You were the one who chose.

368
00:26:48,303 --> 00:26:53,143
Don't you have to give something up
to protect something else?

369
00:26:53,143 --> 00:26:55,303
You're wrong.

370
00:26:55,303 --> 00:26:57,915
It wasn't a sacrifice. It was a mistake.

371
00:26:57,915 --> 00:27:00,039
My mistake was trusting you for a moment

372
00:27:00,039 --> 00:27:03,223
and forgetting what kind of punk you are.

373
00:27:04,115 --> 00:27:06,290
Leave while you're still alive.

374
00:27:07,835 --> 00:27:09,259
Aren't you going to ask this time?

375
00:27:09,259 --> 00:27:11,523
What brings me to Korea?

376
00:27:12,607 --> 00:27:14,895
Just stick to your word.

377
00:27:14,895 --> 00:27:16,756
This is your final warning.

378
00:27:21,315 --> 00:27:24,119
I'll stick to my word.

379
00:27:24,119 --> 00:27:27,656
Because you'll come
looking for me first anyway.

380
00:27:28,839 --> 00:27:30,923
And when that happens,

381
00:27:30,923 --> 00:27:34,956
what choice will you make then, Yoo Bo Na?

382
00:27:40,623 --> 00:27:42,623
[Caller ID Restricted:
You keep your promises well]

383
00:27:44,139 --> 00:27:46,371
[Good. Another good night, Tae Seong]
<i>Goodnight, Tae Seong.</i>

384
00:27:46,371 --> 00:27:49,090
Goodbye, Tae Seong.

385
00:28:05,323 --> 00:28:08,356
[Detective Lee Dong Jin]

386
00:28:15,851 --> 00:28:19,723
Why'd you ask me to come to
such a secluded place?

387
00:28:26,123 --> 00:28:28,056
Are you Kingfisher?

388
00:28:30,056 --> 00:28:32,239
Are you seriously asking me that?

389
00:28:32,239 --> 00:28:34,056
The World Cup case and the Haegong-dong case.

390
00:28:34,056 --> 00:28:36,591
You were there for both major incidents.

391
00:28:36,591 --> 00:28:38,711
The odds of that are practically impossible.

392
00:28:38,711 --> 00:28:40,307
Are you still drunk?

393
00:28:40,307 --> 00:28:42,443
I'm a reporter, you punk!

394
00:28:42,443 --> 00:28:46,556
Tell me. Everything that happened that day.
I'm not joking.

395
00:28:51,151 --> 00:28:55,356
The seven-year-old boy
who was at the scene in Haegong-dong.

396
00:28:55,999 --> 00:28:58,243
What? Why are you bringing that up?

397
00:28:58,243 --> 00:28:59,456
If I didn't know about it,

398
00:28:59,456 --> 00:29:01,779
that means it was never opened up
to the press to protect that kid.

399
00:29:01,779 --> 00:29:03,371
Right, so?

400
00:29:03,371 --> 00:29:06,423
So I have an embargo too.

401
00:29:09,795 --> 00:29:11,495
What?

402
00:29:13,615 --> 00:29:16,256
I have someone I need to protect too.

403
00:29:21,256 --> 00:29:22,923
Let me ask you one thing.

404
00:29:22,923 --> 00:29:27,756
Are you sure the man you saw that day
was Kingfisher?

405
00:29:31,123 --> 00:29:32,411
What about you?

406
00:29:32,411 --> 00:29:36,190
Are you sure Kingfisher knew the son
was there and still pulled the trigger?

407
00:29:42,051 --> 00:29:46,123
I already heard it,
and I can't pretend I haven't.

408
00:29:46,123 --> 00:29:49,267
If that man really was Kingfisher,
then you're a witness.

409
00:29:49,267 --> 00:29:52,523
If not, you could be throwing
the investigation off course. Got it?

410
00:29:53,590 --> 00:29:54,590
I know.

411
00:29:54,590 --> 00:29:56,456
I can't wait long.

412
00:29:56,456 --> 00:29:58,114
Whatever the reason,
figure it out and tell me soon.

413
00:29:58,114 --> 00:30:00,423
Otherwise, I'll force the truth out of you.

414
00:30:01,655 --> 00:30:03,295
You know that, right?

415
00:30:03,295 --> 00:30:04,995
Oh, jeez.

416
00:30:15,123 --> 00:30:19,290
Your wife and your child,

417
00:30:19,995 --> 00:30:22,023
your family could be in danger.

418
00:30:22,023 --> 00:30:28,931
[Four Years Ago, The Night of "That Day"]

419
00:30:31,139 --> 00:30:32,923
Honey, what's wrong?

420
00:30:33,707 --> 00:30:36,711
You're barely eating. Is something wrong?

421
00:30:36,711 --> 00:30:38,903
No.

422
00:30:38,903 --> 00:30:40,603
Nothing's wrong.

423
00:30:42,095 --> 00:30:43,795
This is so good.

424
00:30:45,579 --> 00:30:48,719
By the way, didn't you say
you had something to show me?

425
00:30:48,719 --> 00:30:51,223
- Yeah.
- What is it?

426
00:30:55,407 --> 00:30:56,923
What is it?

427
00:30:56,923 --> 00:30:58,656
Look at this.

428
00:30:59,827 --> 00:31:01,556
What is it?

429
00:31:10,711 --> 00:31:14,123
I went to the hospital today, and I...

430
00:31:20,091 --> 00:31:21,791
<i>What a relief...</i>

431
00:31:22,543 --> 00:31:24,423
<i>to be able to come back.</i>

432
00:31:25,683 --> 00:31:27,383
Tae Seong.

433
00:31:29,559 --> 00:31:31,579
Are you crying?

434
00:31:31,579 --> 00:31:33,695
I'm not.

435
00:31:33,695 --> 00:31:35,971
<i>To come back to you, Bo Na,</i>

436
00:31:35,971 --> 00:31:39,275
<i>and to our baby.</i>

437
00:31:39,275 --> 00:31:41,123
<i>I'm just so relieved.</i>

438
00:31:41,891 --> 00:31:43,803
Are you crying again?

439
00:31:43,803 --> 00:31:44,803
Are you a crybaby?

440
00:31:44,803 --> 00:31:48,079
No, I'm not. I'm just happy. I'm happy.

441
00:31:48,079 --> 00:31:51,656
I'm not crying. Why are you crying?

442
00:32:01,771 --> 00:32:03,990
They said this is the gestational sac.

443
00:32:06,487 --> 00:32:08,263
Oh, my.

444
00:32:22,783 --> 00:32:25,923
Wow! It's orange.

445
00:32:25,923 --> 00:32:27,831
What color will it be?

446
00:32:27,831 --> 00:32:30,187
What's inside the orange?

447
00:32:30,187 --> 00:32:34,107
Ta-da! Wow, it's green.

448
00:32:34,107 --> 00:32:35,107
This is in here too...

449
00:32:35,107 --> 00:32:37,456
<i>Just as I thought,
those two are your Achilles' heels.</i>

450
00:32:37,456 --> 00:32:43,323
Having something to protect
is a fatal weakness for killers like us.

451
00:32:44,899 --> 00:32:47,156
It came out blue!

452
00:32:50,127 --> 00:32:51,687
- Mommy, why?
- Huh?

453
00:32:51,687 --> 00:32:52,907
Mommy, what's wrong?

454
00:32:52,907 --> 00:32:56,735
Mommy? I'm recharging my happiness.

455
00:32:56,735 --> 00:33:00,990
Holding Yul like this
fills Mommy's happiness battery.

456
00:33:00,990 --> 00:33:02,867
Me too! Happiness recharge!

457
00:33:02,867 --> 00:33:04,567
You too?

458
00:33:19,356 --> 00:33:22,323
[Durumi Electronics]

459
00:33:23,583 --> 00:33:25,595
Returned. It was useful.

460
00:33:25,595 --> 00:33:27,447
Just this? What about the others?

461
00:33:27,447 --> 00:33:29,631
I sent those somewhere.

462
00:33:29,631 --> 00:33:32,223
Don't charge it as an expense.
Just bill me for it.

463
00:33:42,587 --> 00:33:44,135
Gwangjang Market?

464
00:33:44,135 --> 00:33:45,890
I guess he was craving
some mung bean pancakes.

465
00:33:45,890 --> 00:33:47,583
So, that ugly mug is here?

466
00:33:47,583 --> 00:33:48,787
Tracking down restaurants?

467
00:33:48,787 --> 00:33:51,095
It doesn't look like he came
all this way just for a food tour.

468
00:33:51,095 --> 00:33:53,123
Please share this with me.

469
00:34:00,535 --> 00:34:03,236
Oh, that looks good.

470
00:34:03,236 --> 00:34:04,936
[Incoming Call]

471
00:34:07,047 --> 00:34:08,099
Not here.

472
00:34:08,099 --> 00:34:09,691
Looks like they got away.

473
00:34:09,691 --> 00:34:12,990
And Yoo Bo Na doesn't seem to know yet.

474
00:34:15,815 --> 00:34:17,531
Me?

475
00:34:17,531 --> 00:34:19,323
Well, since I'm here,

476
00:34:19,323 --> 00:34:22,456
maybe I'll check out some
good restaurants nearby.

477
00:34:22,456 --> 00:34:24,456
There are tons of great places
to eat in Korea.

478
00:34:27,907 --> 00:34:29,607
Mr. Kwon!

479
00:34:30,971 --> 00:34:32,775
Mr. Kwon!

480
00:34:32,775 --> 00:34:34,011
Yeah?

481
00:34:34,011 --> 00:34:38,256
What were you thinking about so deeply
that you didn't even hear me calling?

482
00:34:39,271 --> 00:34:42,419
Well, if you heard a voice again that
you first heard four years ago,

483
00:34:42,419 --> 00:34:44,519
do you think you'd recognize it?

484
00:34:44,519 --> 00:34:46,219
Huh?

485
00:34:47,579 --> 00:34:49,011
I'm not sure.

486
00:34:49,011 --> 00:34:54,419
Maybe if it's a familiar voice I hear
all the time, like a singer or actor,

487
00:34:55,255 --> 00:34:57,535
but just hearing it once? That's tough.

488
00:34:57,535 --> 00:34:59,956
Why do you ask?

489
00:35:00,623 --> 00:35:02,323
Never mind.

490
00:35:03,623 --> 00:35:05,831
Let's get to the meeting.

491
00:35:05,831 --> 00:35:10,251
Did you find out how many of
the parolees were violent offenders?

492
00:35:10,251 --> 00:35:13,175
I pulled the data from the past
ten years and analyzed it.

493
00:35:13,175 --> 00:35:15,963
[Number of Parolees by Violent Crime Type]
It's broken down by violent crime type,

494
00:35:15,963 --> 00:35:18,667
including murder, drugs, and sexual assault.

495
00:35:18,667 --> 00:35:22,923
And this is a separate list of
violent offenders released this year.

496
00:35:23,856 --> 00:35:26,556
You must've spent days on this.

497
00:35:27,790 --> 00:35:29,656
[2026 Violent Offenders Released on Parole]

498
00:35:30,590 --> 00:35:32,856
[Jang Eun Hak, Assault Resulting in Death]

499
00:35:35,343 --> 00:35:38,323
Mr. Kwon, what's wrong? Are you okay?

500
00:35:41,523 --> 00:35:44,223
[Model Prisoner]

501
00:35:58,331 --> 00:35:59,739
<i>What about you?</i>

502
00:35:59,739 --> 00:36:03,423
<i>Are you sure Kingfisher knew the son
was there and still pulled the trigger?</i>

503
00:36:07,967 --> 00:36:09,667
Mr. Lee!

504
00:36:10,343 --> 00:36:12,459
I got the victim statements
from the couple assault case.

505
00:36:12,459 --> 00:36:14,547
What should I do? Should I ask
the cybercrime unit for assistance?

506
00:36:14,547 --> 00:36:16,751
Yeah, go ahead.
And let me know if you find anything.

507
00:36:16,751 --> 00:36:18,451
Alright.

508
00:36:21,375 --> 00:36:23,756
What are you looking at so intently...

509
00:36:24,795 --> 00:36:26,207
The Haegong-dong Gosiwon?

510
00:36:26,207 --> 00:36:27,907
Why this case?

511
00:36:29,171 --> 00:36:30,199
Why aren't you asking me about it?

512
00:36:30,199 --> 00:36:32,139
About what?

513
00:36:32,139 --> 00:36:35,395
Oh, you mean the part about him
being killed in front of his son?

514
00:36:35,395 --> 00:36:37,067
That's just speculation, you know.

515
00:36:37,067 --> 00:36:40,001
Honestly, I don't think Kingfisher
would have pulled the trigger

516
00:36:40,001 --> 00:36:42,147
knowing there was a kid there.

517
00:36:42,147 --> 00:36:43,747
Well, look here.

518
00:36:43,747 --> 00:36:45,587
The windows in a Gosiwon
are pretty small, right?

519
00:36:45,587 --> 00:36:49,690
Couldn't there have been a blind spot
from the sniper's position?

520
00:36:54,539 --> 00:36:56,395
Beom.

521
00:36:56,395 --> 00:36:58,771
Leave work early today.

522
00:36:58,771 --> 00:37:00,471
Leave work?

523
00:37:01,075 --> 00:37:02,435
Are you telling me to go home?

524
00:37:02,435 --> 00:37:04,319
[Reporter Kwon Tae Seong]
You mean, not working late?

525
00:37:04,319 --> 00:37:06,923
Then do you want to work late?

526
00:37:06,923 --> 00:37:08,990
You're sure it's okay?

527
00:37:10,311 --> 00:37:11,311
Yay!

528
00:37:11,311 --> 00:37:12,623
No taking it back, okay?

529
00:37:12,623 --> 00:37:16,056
Then I'll stop by the cybercrime unit
and head straight home.

530
00:37:17,799 --> 00:37:19,499
Sir, yes, sir!

531
00:37:20,567 --> 00:37:23,123
- Hey, where are you going?
- I'm going home! I'm off!

532
00:37:23,923 --> 00:37:25,823
[Reporter Kwon Tae Seong]

533
00:37:26,831 --> 00:37:29,023
Is the embargo over already?

534
00:37:30,243 --> 00:37:32,656
If you're calling me,
just say what's up. What is it?

535
00:37:32,656 --> 00:37:33,656
Dong Jin.

536
00:37:33,656 --> 00:37:37,311
Why are you calling me so sweetly?
You're making me nervous.

537
00:37:37,311 --> 00:37:39,290
<i>What's up? What's happening?</i>

538
00:37:40,411 --> 00:37:41,735
That punk's been released.

539
00:37:41,735 --> 00:37:44,863
That punk? Which punk?

540
00:37:44,863 --> 00:37:47,090
He was released on parole a month ago.

541
00:37:50,155 --> 00:37:51,855
What?

542
00:37:54,290 --> 00:37:58,735
<i>The so-called Gangmyeon-dong
Supermarket Murder Case.</i>

543
00:37:58,735 --> 00:38:00,631
[Client Information]
The perpetrator, Jang Eun Hak,

544
00:38:00,631 --> 00:38:02,475
brutally murdered a married couple

545
00:38:02,475 --> 00:38:05,375
who ran a neighborhood supermarket
with a broken soju bottle,

546
00:38:05,375 --> 00:38:07,847
fled the scene,
and was caught four years later.

547
00:38:07,847 --> 00:38:12,117
He was sentenced to 16 years in prison,
but he was paroled last month,

548
00:38:12,117 --> 00:38:14,556
just one year before his sentence
was due to end.

549
00:38:14,556 --> 00:38:15,803
[Dongwoon Furniture]
Hello.

550
00:38:15,803 --> 00:38:17,856
Oh, hello.

551
00:38:19,156 --> 00:38:20,496
- Are you looking for a bed?
- Yeah.

552
00:38:20,496 --> 00:38:23,090
What size bed are you looking for?

553
00:38:28,787 --> 00:38:30,775
Mr. Jang!

554
00:38:30,775 --> 00:38:32,043
Mr. Jang!

555
00:38:32,043 --> 00:38:35,027
- Oh, yeah.
- Move that.

556
00:38:35,027 --> 00:38:37,290
Oh, yes, understood.

557
00:38:38,939 --> 00:38:41,423
Oh, dear.

558
00:38:42,451 --> 00:38:46,527
Two people were brutally murdered,
and he only got 16 years?

559
00:38:46,527 --> 00:38:47,547
What?

560
00:38:47,547 --> 00:38:50,739
He was convicted of death resulting
from assault, not murder?

561
00:38:50,739 --> 00:38:51,767
That's right.

562
00:38:51,767 --> 00:38:53,371
He was 100 won short for soju,

563
00:38:53,371 --> 00:38:55,963
got into a scuffle,
and ended up committing murder.

564
00:38:55,963 --> 00:39:00,203
Then in court, he begged and pleaded,
claiming he was drunk and felt humiliated,

565
00:39:00,203 --> 00:39:03,419
so he did what he did.

566
00:39:03,419 --> 00:39:05,335
He exploited the leniency of the law.

567
00:39:05,335 --> 00:39:06,591
They say the law has mercy.

568
00:39:06,591 --> 00:39:10,727
Jeez, the victims' families
shed tears of blood.

569
00:39:10,727 --> 00:39:13,091
They do.

570
00:39:13,091 --> 00:39:15,056
Tears that never dry.

571
00:39:17,915 --> 00:39:22,756
But there's one notable detail there.

572
00:39:23,595 --> 00:39:27,831
<i>The victim's family has a son,</i>

573
00:39:27,831 --> 00:39:31,390
[Lee Dong Jin, 17 at the time]
and he's a detective.

574
00:39:32,443 --> 00:39:35,731
What's even more interesting is that

575
00:39:35,731 --> 00:39:38,290
he was once assigned to a Kingfisher case.

576
00:39:39,635 --> 00:39:42,096
Wow, what an irony.

577
00:39:42,096 --> 00:39:45,995
A police officer whose family was
victimized by a crime, chasing Kingfisher.

578
00:39:45,995 --> 00:39:48,619
With such a light sentence,
he must be devastated to find out

579
00:39:48,619 --> 00:39:50,075
the guy even got parole.

580
00:39:50,075 --> 00:39:52,490
Not devastated. Furious.

581
00:39:53,488 --> 00:39:55,743
Do you think he might do something dangerous?

582
00:39:55,743 --> 00:39:56,783
I know.

583
00:39:56,783 --> 00:40:00,090
He's a cop, and he has a gun.

584
00:40:00,771 --> 00:40:03,090
No. He's not that kind of person.

585
00:40:03,767 --> 00:40:07,419
If he wanted personal revenge,
he wouldn't have become a cop.

586
00:40:07,419 --> 00:40:10,607
He believes in making criminals pay
within the law.

587
00:40:10,607 --> 00:40:12,423
That's what the police are there for.

588
00:40:23,990 --> 00:40:27,090
[Seoul Nambu Police Station, Lee Dong Jin]

589
00:40:31,891 --> 00:40:33,535
Se Ah.

590
00:40:33,535 --> 00:40:34,635
A date?

591
00:40:34,635 --> 00:40:36,590
Just the two of us?

592
00:40:37,547 --> 00:40:40,071
Really? Then where should we meet?

593
00:40:40,071 --> 00:40:42,047
Meeting one-on-one outside...

594
00:40:42,047 --> 00:40:44,815
Classic sister-in-law move,
summoning her brother's wife like this.

595
00:40:44,815 --> 00:40:47,847
Still, isn't a sister-in-law easier
to deal with than a mother-in-law?

596
00:40:47,847 --> 00:40:51,106
There's a reason they say
a meddling sister-in-law is even worse.

597
00:40:51,106 --> 00:40:55,256
She's in trouble, or she's about to be.

598
00:41:07,775 --> 00:41:09,927
If you find anything,
please let me know right away.

599
00:41:09,927 --> 00:41:11,627
Sir, yes, sir!

600
00:41:18,319 --> 00:41:21,423
<i>I'm leaving work on time
for the first time in a million years.</i>

601
00:41:21,423 --> 00:41:22,959
Want to hit the arcade?

602
00:41:22,959 --> 00:41:24,807
<i>Nope. I've got a date.</i>

603
00:41:24,807 --> 00:41:26,507
A date?

604
00:41:27,921 --> 00:41:29,002
With a guy?

605
00:41:29,002 --> 00:41:30,702
<i>With my sister-in-law.</i>

606
00:41:31,327 --> 00:41:33,356
Figures.

607
00:41:36,147 --> 00:41:38,739
Then what should I do?

608
00:41:38,739 --> 00:41:39,851
Bo Na, over here.

609
00:41:39,851 --> 00:41:42,183
They say this place is seriously good.

610
00:41:42,183 --> 00:41:44,227
- Wow!
- Looks like there's no line today.

611
00:41:44,227 --> 00:41:46,070
- Welcome.
- Table for two.

612
00:41:46,070 --> 00:41:47,716
- Do you have a reservation?
- No.

613
00:41:47,716 --> 00:41:50,559
You have to book through
our app before you come.

614
00:41:50,559 --> 00:41:52,715
- Through an app?
- Yeah, I'm sorry.

615
00:41:52,715 --> 00:41:55,051
Then would you like to wait?

616
00:41:55,051 --> 00:41:56,751
[Waitlist]
Wait...

617
00:41:57,375 --> 00:41:58,403
There are like 20 people waiting.

618
00:41:58,403 --> 00:41:59,923
- What do we do?
- Number 35!

619
00:41:59,923 --> 00:42:02,023
- Yes.
- This way, please.

620
00:42:03,327 --> 00:42:04,559
Thank you.

621
00:42:04,559 --> 00:42:05,590
Enjoy your food.

622
00:42:05,590 --> 00:42:06,790
Start with this, like this.

623
00:42:06,790 --> 00:42:08,390
Oh, Bo Na, wait.

624
00:42:08,390 --> 00:42:10,390
No? Right now...

625
00:42:16,207 --> 00:42:18,956
Bo Na, should we take a picture together?

626
00:42:21,090 --> 00:42:22,290
<i>Don't look at the camera.</i>

627
00:42:22,290 --> 00:42:23,923
<i>Yes, pretend you're not
looking and act casual.</i>

628
00:42:23,923 --> 00:42:25,311
Try to look as pretty as possible.

629
00:42:25,311 --> 00:42:27,847
Two? Give me a pretty pose!

630
00:42:27,847 --> 00:42:29,156
- That's so cute.
- Ta-da!

631
00:42:29,156 --> 00:42:30,345
How is it?

632
00:42:30,345 --> 00:42:31,656
Oh, my, you look like a bunny!

633
00:42:31,656 --> 00:42:33,856
- How do you do this? A heart.
- A heart.

634
00:42:38,683 --> 00:42:41,883
Mom, you're really something else, huh?

635
00:42:41,883 --> 00:42:45,935
You badmouth Bo Na,
but you still make her all those side dishes.

636
00:42:45,935 --> 00:42:48,751
Oh, please. What are you talking about?

637
00:42:48,751 --> 00:42:50,575
Am I doing it for her?

638
00:42:50,575 --> 00:42:53,575
I make it to feed my own son.

639
00:42:53,575 --> 00:42:57,290
Oh, dear. Other mothers-in-law
pack all kinds of food

640
00:42:57,290 --> 00:42:59,071
for their sons-in-law.

641
00:42:59,071 --> 00:43:01,055
Jeez, there you go again.

642
00:43:01,055 --> 00:43:03,259
- I'm exhausted.
- Oh, you're here?

643
00:43:03,259 --> 00:43:04,963
Sun Il, please get me a glass of water.

644
00:43:04,963 --> 00:43:06,575
Alright.

645
00:43:06,575 --> 00:43:07,751
Where did you go?

646
00:43:07,751 --> 00:43:09,739
Oh, the department store.

647
00:43:09,739 --> 00:43:13,207
You know we're meeting Jun Woo's
future in-laws the day after tomorrow.

648
00:43:13,207 --> 00:43:16,156
Oh, right. Your second son's
wedding date is set.

649
00:43:16,156 --> 00:43:17,156
But why the department store?

650
00:43:17,156 --> 00:43:19,927
Well, I need something decent to wear.

651
00:43:19,927 --> 00:43:23,239
Seon Ja, what did you wear for
Tae Seong's family meeting?

652
00:43:23,239 --> 00:43:24,791
What?

653
00:43:24,791 --> 00:43:27,031
Well, just something simple.

654
00:43:27,031 --> 00:43:29,675
Oh, right. You never had one, did you?

655
00:43:29,675 --> 00:43:32,671
Oh, lucky you. You had it easy.

656
00:43:32,671 --> 00:43:34,119
Oh, my back.

657
00:43:34,119 --> 00:43:35,715
What do you mean I didn't have one?

658
00:43:35,715 --> 00:43:38,867
I did it twice for Sun Il and Du Ri.

659
00:43:38,867 --> 00:43:43,023
Is meeting your daughter's in-laws
the same as meeting your son's?

660
00:43:44,331 --> 00:43:47,390
They're basically the same.

661
00:43:48,590 --> 00:43:52,535
You can tell what kind of family
you're dealing with by meeting the parents.

662
00:43:52,535 --> 00:43:55,951
Both of our future in-laws are educators.

663
00:43:55,951 --> 00:43:59,831
Maybe that's why their daughter
is so well-mannered,

664
00:43:59,831 --> 00:44:02,483
and her face is so bright, without a shadow.

665
00:44:02,483 --> 00:44:06,190
You can just tell
she grew up surrounded by love.

666
00:44:07,091 --> 00:44:11,027
Oh, dear. Is it a little awkward
saying this in front of you?

667
00:44:11,027 --> 00:44:12,356
- Your daughter-in-law...
- You punk!

668
00:44:12,356 --> 00:44:13,723
- Shut your mouth!
- Oh, my.

669
00:44:13,723 --> 00:44:14,890
Oh, my, what's gotten into you?

670
00:44:14,890 --> 00:44:16,587
Oh, my. What did I even do?

671
00:44:16,587 --> 00:44:20,327
Fine. I never had a formal family meeting,
and I don't have any in-laws.

672
00:44:20,327 --> 00:44:22,090
Because my daughter-in-law is an orphan.

673
00:44:22,090 --> 00:44:24,019
So what? What about it?

674
00:44:24,019 --> 00:44:25,851
Did you contribute anything?

675
00:44:25,851 --> 00:44:28,631
Well, I gave quite a lot
for the wedding gift.

676
00:44:28,631 --> 00:44:31,895
Why are you making such a fuss over
getting an orphaned daughter-in-law?

677
00:44:31,895 --> 00:44:34,483
Wow, I've been friends
with you all my life...

678
00:44:34,483 --> 00:44:36,371
You little punk. I'm going to get you today.

679
00:44:36,371 --> 00:44:37,623
Oh, my. Oh, my!

680
00:44:37,623 --> 00:44:39,523
- Mom!
- What's gotten into you?

681
00:44:42,467 --> 00:44:44,167
Wow!

682
00:44:47,623 --> 00:44:51,175
Se Ah, what do you usually do
when you hang out with your friends?

683
00:44:51,175 --> 00:44:52,415
Me?

684
00:44:52,415 --> 00:44:56,890
We'd go for chicken feet and soju.
Or cold pork belly and beer.

685
00:44:58,875 --> 00:45:00,623
Was it that obvious?

686
00:45:02,190 --> 00:45:05,704
Actually, I did some research before I came.

687
00:45:05,704 --> 00:45:08,856
I was wondering what young people
do for fun these days.

688
00:45:08,856 --> 00:45:11,390
Like the place we went to earlier.

689
00:45:11,390 --> 00:45:16,390
It's not really my thing,
but I thought you might enjoy it.

690
00:45:17,319 --> 00:45:19,790
So it was your first time.

691
00:45:22,556 --> 00:45:27,790
I actually love just sitting around
doing nothing with you.

692
00:45:28,856 --> 00:45:29,931
Really?

693
00:45:29,931 --> 00:45:31,690
Yeah.

694
00:45:34,331 --> 00:45:37,583
Then where do you actually go most often?

695
00:45:37,583 --> 00:45:39,262
Let's have that be our last stop.

696
00:45:39,262 --> 00:45:40,962
Is that what you want?

697
00:45:42,207 --> 00:45:45,023
There's one place.

698
00:45:48,023 --> 00:45:50,090
[Se Dol, You Have a New Message]

699
00:45:54,439 --> 00:45:57,056
<i>Get to the PC bang now.</i>

700
00:46:03,431 --> 00:46:05,023
Hey, why are you so late?

701
00:46:05,023 --> 00:46:06,456
You said you were leaving work on time.

702
00:46:06,456 --> 00:46:08,187
Huh?

703
00:46:08,187 --> 00:46:12,619
I went somewhere else first.
What, you think you're my only friend?

704
00:46:12,619 --> 00:46:14,690
Hey, say hi. This is my sister-in-law.

705
00:46:14,690 --> 00:46:16,579
Bo Na, this is my friend, Mr. Tiger.

706
00:46:16,579 --> 00:46:18,556
- Hello.
- Oh, hi.

707
00:46:18,556 --> 00:46:20,256
I didn't know your friend was a guy.

708
00:46:20,256 --> 00:46:21,423
Is he your boyfriend?

709
00:46:21,423 --> 00:46:23,596
No, we're just friends.

710
00:46:23,596 --> 00:46:25,687
Nice to meet you properly.

711
00:46:25,687 --> 00:46:27,187
I'm Beom Seong Hun.

712
00:46:27,187 --> 00:46:29,390
I'm really sorry
I couldn't make it to the wedding.

713
00:46:29,390 --> 00:46:32,179
Oh, don't be.

714
00:46:32,179 --> 00:46:34,556
- He's handsome.
- What?

715
00:46:35,611 --> 00:46:38,056
Then, let's skip the formalities
and sit down.

716
00:46:38,056 --> 00:46:40,695
Alright, your only mission today is

717
00:46:40,695 --> 00:46:45,072
to show my sister-in-law
the true taste of victory. Got it?

718
00:46:45,072 --> 00:46:47,490
Well, that's a lot of weight on my shoulders.

719
00:46:47,490 --> 00:46:49,390
I'm counting on you.

720
00:46:50,395 --> 00:46:53,799
Bo Na, since my friend's here,
want to try an FPS game?

721
00:46:53,799 --> 00:46:55,035
FPS?

722
00:46:55,035 --> 00:46:59,511
When you're stressed,
nothing beats shooting things.

723
00:46:59,511 --> 00:47:01,159
Bang, bang!

724
00:47:01,159 --> 00:47:03,091
Sniping.

725
00:47:03,091 --> 00:47:05,283
There's a game where you snipe people?

726
00:47:05,283 --> 00:47:08,690
Yeah, it's a little difficult.

727
00:47:08,690 --> 00:47:11,090
But you can just stick with us,
and you'll be fine.

728
00:47:11,090 --> 00:47:14,811
He'll do all the killing anyway.

729
00:47:14,811 --> 00:47:15,923
Please take care of me.

730
00:47:15,923 --> 00:47:16,923
Oh, come on.

731
00:47:16,923 --> 00:47:19,456
I'm not that good.

732
00:47:19,456 --> 00:47:21,523
Okay, shall we give it a try?

733
00:47:21,523 --> 00:47:23,223
Sure.

734
00:47:25,991 --> 00:47:28,799
There, there's someone over there.
SW 1 direction.

735
00:47:28,799 --> 00:47:30,131
Oh, okay, got it.

736
00:47:30,131 --> 00:47:32,071
Oh, nice.

737
00:47:32,071 --> 00:47:33,379
Well, it's nothing.

738
00:47:33,379 --> 00:47:34,643
Watch out, there's one more.

739
00:47:34,643 --> 00:47:37,371
Hey, behind that wall. See him?

740
00:47:37,371 --> 00:47:39,075
Wow, what's gotten into you?

741
00:47:39,075 --> 00:47:40,090
Hey, ping one, ping one.

742
00:47:40,090 --> 00:47:42,356
Oh, yeah! Assist!

743
00:47:42,356 --> 00:47:44,356
Oh, your aim is really good today.

744
00:47:44,356 --> 00:47:46,256
What's with the sudden praise?

745
00:47:47,979 --> 00:47:50,756
Oh, why are you so good today?

746
00:47:50,756 --> 00:47:51,883
I'll take care of him.

747
00:47:51,883 --> 00:47:54,323
- One team left, one team.
- Okay.

748
00:47:54,323 --> 00:47:57,723
I smell chicken.

749
00:47:57,723 --> 00:47:58,823
What is it?

750
00:47:58,823 --> 00:48:00,423
This feels like a chicken dinner.

751
00:48:00,423 --> 00:48:03,190
[Match in progress in the marked zone.
45 seconds left]

752
00:48:03,190 --> 00:48:04,923
Chicken!

753
00:48:06,256 --> 00:48:07,823
Bo Na, how was it? Winning's fun, right?

754
00:48:07,823 --> 00:48:10,390
It's so much fun.

755
00:48:11,356 --> 00:48:12,419
This is really fun.

756
00:48:12,419 --> 00:48:13,695
- Right?
- Yeah.

757
00:48:13,695 --> 00:48:18,815
Hey, thanks to you,
my years of pent-up stress are gone!

758
00:48:18,815 --> 00:48:20,419
You were great.

759
00:48:20,419 --> 00:48:21,687
No, it wasn't me.

760
00:48:21,687 --> 00:48:23,387
What do you mean?

761
00:48:25,299 --> 00:48:26,611
[We Won! Chicken for Dinner Tonight!]
What?

762
00:48:26,611 --> 00:48:28,267
Three kills?

763
00:48:28,267 --> 00:48:29,747
You only got three kills?

764
00:48:29,747 --> 00:48:31,675
Then, how did we even win?

765
00:48:31,675 --> 00:48:33,507
Come with me.

766
00:48:33,507 --> 00:48:35,587
[Team Rank 1, 15 Kills]
Huh?

767
00:48:35,587 --> 00:48:38,083
Bo Na, what is this?

768
00:48:38,083 --> 00:48:39,275
What?

769
00:48:39,275 --> 00:48:41,827
You got all those kills!

770
00:48:41,827 --> 00:48:43,087
This isn't your first time, is it?

771
00:48:43,087 --> 00:48:45,535
I think we just discovered
your hidden talent.

772
00:48:45,535 --> 00:48:49,190
Were you a sniper in a past life?

773
00:48:49,190 --> 00:48:50,190
Maybe I was.

774
00:48:50,190 --> 00:48:53,491
- This is amazing!
- I guess I got lucky today.

775
00:48:53,491 --> 00:48:55,739
Well, let's play one more round.

776
00:48:55,739 --> 00:48:57,056
- You want to?
- Yeah.

777
00:48:57,056 --> 00:48:58,423
Alright.

778
00:48:58,423 --> 00:49:00,390
This game isn't exactly easy.

779
00:49:00,390 --> 00:49:03,090
[13 Kills, 14 Kills, 16 Kills]

780
00:49:04,434 --> 00:49:06,134
[17 Kills]

781
00:49:14,582 --> 00:49:16,282
Oh, dear.

782
00:49:20,256 --> 00:49:22,507
[Team Rank 1, 19 Kills]

783
00:49:22,507 --> 00:49:23,735
Wow...

784
00:49:23,735 --> 00:49:25,423
No way...

785
00:49:25,423 --> 00:49:27,990
This isn't possible.

786
00:49:29,415 --> 00:49:34,090
Se Ah must've been enjoying herself
to keep you out that late.

787
00:49:34,090 --> 00:49:36,390
I had so much fun.

788
00:49:36,390 --> 00:49:39,291
I got to try a lot of things
I'd never done before. It was really fun.

789
00:49:39,291 --> 00:49:42,091
<i>Looks like Se Ah really did
something big today.</i>

790
00:49:42,091 --> 00:49:45,056
It's okay. Take your time.

791
00:49:45,056 --> 00:49:47,623
<i>I'm going to take Yul to the store later.</i>

792
00:49:47,623 --> 00:49:48,959
Sun Il said to bring over some fresh kimchi.

793
00:49:48,959 --> 00:49:51,111
Really? I love your mom's fresh kimchi.

794
00:49:51,111 --> 00:49:52,491
Please bring lots.

795
00:49:52,491 --> 00:49:57,391
Today I discovered a side of my sister-in-law
that completely blew me away.

796
00:49:57,391 --> 00:49:58,859
Isn't she seriously cool?

797
00:49:58,859 --> 00:50:01,563
How old is your brother's kid again?

798
00:50:01,563 --> 00:50:04,387
Yul? Four? Why do you ask that?

799
00:50:04,387 --> 00:50:07,223
Then the timing lines up perfectly, huh?

800
00:50:08,235 --> 00:50:09,590
You know I have a good gut feeling, right?

801
00:50:09,590 --> 00:50:11,911
What, you?

802
00:50:11,911 --> 00:50:14,056
I think your sister-in-law...

803
00:50:16,387 --> 00:50:18,711
might be hiding her true identity.

804
00:50:18,711 --> 00:50:20,703
What identity?

805
00:50:20,703 --> 00:50:24,223
The legend who vanished without a trace
in the spring four years ago...

806
00:50:26,551 --> 00:50:28,199
the legend of FPS games!

807
00:50:28,199 --> 00:50:30,590
But she was on maternity leave.

808
00:50:30,590 --> 00:50:34,491
A gaming genius who shows up
every few years and sweeps the top records?

809
00:50:34,491 --> 00:50:36,090
Enough with the nonsense!

810
00:50:36,090 --> 00:50:38,175
Okay.

811
00:50:38,175 --> 00:50:39,875
Well...

812
00:50:42,239 --> 00:50:46,723
Bo Na, were you surprised
when I suddenly asked you out today?

813
00:50:46,723 --> 00:50:50,619
No. I was just... excited.

814
00:50:50,619 --> 00:50:54,479
It's been so long since I've gone out
and had fun without Yul. It was exciting.

815
00:50:54,479 --> 00:50:56,011
Really?

816
00:50:56,011 --> 00:51:00,243
So you haven't really seen
your friends since you had Yul?

817
00:51:00,243 --> 00:51:03,163
I guess I don't really have many friends.

818
00:51:03,163 --> 00:51:04,556
I'm not sure why.

819
00:51:04,556 --> 00:51:07,127
Oh, I see.

820
00:51:07,127 --> 00:51:11,635
I feel like I got a little
closer to you today.

821
00:51:11,635 --> 00:51:13,527
You do?

822
00:51:13,527 --> 00:51:17,971
Actually, there was something
I wanted to ask you.

823
00:51:17,971 --> 00:51:21,299
That's partly why I asked you out.

824
00:51:21,299 --> 00:51:23,611
But I've changed my mind.

825
00:51:23,611 --> 00:51:25,755
I'm going to ask you for something else!

826
00:51:25,755 --> 00:51:26,967
What is it?

827
00:51:26,967 --> 00:51:31,779
From now on, please speak casually with me.

828
00:51:31,779 --> 00:51:36,523
I'm Tae Seong's younger sister,
and we're family.

829
00:51:38,187 --> 00:51:39,975
Okay, should we do that then?

830
00:51:39,975 --> 00:51:41,519
Really? Oh, yeah!

831
00:51:41,519 --> 00:51:43,011
What a rewarding day!

832
00:51:43,011 --> 00:51:46,023
Then can I link arms with you?

833
00:51:46,023 --> 00:51:47,187
Sure, come here.

834
00:51:47,187 --> 00:51:49,190
Oh, really?

835
00:51:51,803 --> 00:51:53,656
This is nice!

836
00:51:53,656 --> 00:51:55,456
[Tae Seong Chicken]

837
00:51:55,456 --> 00:51:58,783
Mom, are you still mad?

838
00:51:58,783 --> 00:52:00,319
You really hold a grudge.

839
00:52:00,319 --> 00:52:03,656
Come on, it's not like her saying
rude things is anything new.

840
00:52:03,656 --> 00:52:06,611
Still, you don't like it when others
badmouth your daughter-in-law, do you?

841
00:52:06,611 --> 00:52:09,141
Of course I don't, huh?

842
00:52:09,141 --> 00:52:10,659
She's my daughter now too.

843
00:52:10,659 --> 00:52:13,815
If anyone's going to criticize her,
it should be me. Who is she?

844
00:52:13,815 --> 00:52:16,775
What, "bright"?

845
00:52:16,775 --> 00:52:18,599
Is that supposed to mean
my girl is dark and dull?

846
00:52:18,599 --> 00:52:20,490
Oh, my. "My girl"?

847
00:52:20,490 --> 00:52:22,015
That darn punk.

848
00:52:22,015 --> 00:52:23,951
Who's bragging?

849
00:52:23,951 --> 00:52:26,070
I hated the orphan daughter-in-law too,

850
00:52:26,070 --> 00:52:28,647
and I was annoyed about
not having a meeting with her family.

851
00:52:28,647 --> 00:52:31,647
- Mom!
- What mom in this world

852
00:52:31,647 --> 00:52:34,790
wants to give her precious son to an orphan?

853
00:52:34,790 --> 00:52:36,235
But as time went by...

854
00:52:36,235 --> 00:52:38,056
Mom!

855
00:52:50,071 --> 00:52:52,218
Oh, you're here?

856
00:52:52,218 --> 00:52:53,918
Yes, Mother.

857
00:52:55,359 --> 00:52:58,190
Wait, how are you two together again...

858
00:53:01,214 --> 00:53:03,090
Honey, take Yul outside first.

859
00:53:03,090 --> 00:53:04,090
Huh?

860
00:53:04,090 --> 00:53:06,523
Please. Just go. I'm asking you.

861
00:53:08,019 --> 00:53:09,423
[Red Bean Bread]
Mother, have this when you get hungry.

862
00:53:09,423 --> 00:53:10,431
It's your favorite red bean bread.

863
00:53:10,431 --> 00:53:13,456
Oh, okay. Thank you.

864
00:53:23,190 --> 00:53:25,356
[Red Bean Bread]

865
00:53:27,423 --> 00:53:31,356
You should've told me
you were bringing her with you.

866
00:53:32,587 --> 00:53:34,923
Did you eat dinner?

867
00:53:37,007 --> 00:53:39,219
Mom.

868
00:53:39,219 --> 00:53:41,190
Apologize to Yul's mom.

869
00:53:41,190 --> 00:53:45,999
Well, I didn't say it for her to hear.

870
00:53:45,999 --> 00:53:48,090
But she heard you.

871
00:53:49,707 --> 00:53:52,835
Did I make anything up?

872
00:53:52,835 --> 00:53:55,267
She is an orphan.

873
00:53:55,267 --> 00:53:57,111
Mom!

874
00:53:57,111 --> 00:54:00,231
Just because she's an orphan doesn't mean
you can treat her however you want.

875
00:54:00,231 --> 00:54:02,923
What did I do...

876
00:54:05,805 --> 00:54:09,477
So what? What if I say I can't apologize?

877
00:54:09,477 --> 00:54:12,256
What? Are you going to stop seeing me?

878
00:54:25,935 --> 00:54:30,086
Jeez, they say raising kids is useless.

879
00:54:30,086 --> 00:54:33,535
All you care about is
how precious your wife is.

880
00:54:33,535 --> 00:54:35,235
Mom.

881
00:54:35,923 --> 00:54:37,399
Mom, honestly, you're sorry, aren't you?

882
00:54:37,399 --> 00:54:39,599
Sorry for what?

883
00:54:39,599 --> 00:54:42,990
People even talk bad about the president
in private. What's the big deal?

884
00:54:44,387 --> 00:54:48,190
Why did they have to walk in
at that exact moment and make such a fuss?

885
00:54:49,891 --> 00:54:52,956
What lousy timing.

886
00:54:59,159 --> 00:55:00,447
I'm sorry.

887
00:55:00,447 --> 00:55:02,723
I'll apologize on her behalf.

888
00:55:04,351 --> 00:55:07,431
Me? I'm fine.

889
00:55:07,431 --> 00:55:09,523
It doesn't bother me.

890
00:55:12,495 --> 00:55:14,756
She's your mom.

891
00:55:14,756 --> 00:55:16,190
Maybe it's because I'm a mom too?

892
00:55:16,190 --> 00:55:19,856
I think I understand a little.

893
00:55:20,868 --> 00:55:23,690
That feeling of being helpless
in front of your child.

894
00:55:24,339 --> 00:55:27,956
That instinct to put your child first.

895
00:55:32,967 --> 00:55:37,090
Being a mom doesn't excuse everything.
She was still wrong.

896
00:55:40,759 --> 00:55:44,095
Then should I tell you exactly what I think?

897
00:55:44,095 --> 00:55:46,456
Isn't your mom being a little too much?

898
00:55:47,790 --> 00:55:51,171
Well, I'm not the person I used to be.

899
00:55:51,171 --> 00:55:52,575
I'm not alone anymore.

900
00:55:52,575 --> 00:55:54,590
I have a husband and a daughter.

901
00:55:54,590 --> 00:55:58,027
I have a mother-in-law
and three sisters-in-law.

902
00:55:58,027 --> 00:56:01,356
What matters is the present,
not the past. Isn't it?

903
00:56:05,463 --> 00:56:07,163
But...

904
00:56:08,323 --> 00:56:11,356
I believe she'll understand someday.

905
00:56:11,356 --> 00:56:13,990
If we keep arguing and making up like this...

906
00:56:15,490 --> 00:56:17,723
Look at you, saying things like that.

907
00:56:18,423 --> 00:56:22,179
I mean, we laugh and cry together,

908
00:56:22,179 --> 00:56:26,711
get on each other's nerves,
hurt each other...

909
00:56:26,711 --> 00:56:28,856
Isn't that what family is?

910
00:56:29,635 --> 00:56:32,956
So we're really going at it.

911
00:56:34,331 --> 00:56:36,590
Going at it? What are we going at?

912
00:56:37,391 --> 00:56:39,374
What do you want to eat, Yul?

913
00:56:39,374 --> 00:56:41,319
Should we stir-fry Yul's favorite sausages?

914
00:56:41,319 --> 00:56:43,423
Yeah, I like sausages.

915
00:56:43,423 --> 00:56:44,790
Let's go stir-fry some sausages.

916
00:56:44,790 --> 00:56:47,490
Let's go make some sausages!

917
00:57:13,787 --> 00:57:16,123
Why are the lights off?

918
00:57:16,123 --> 00:57:17,990
Are they closed already?

919
00:57:21,390 --> 00:57:24,856
The door isn't even locked. What's going on?

920
00:57:49,835 --> 00:57:51,656
Mom.

921
00:57:51,656 --> 00:57:53,356
Mom.

922
00:57:54,056 --> 00:57:55,790
Dad.

923
00:58:16,690 --> 00:58:19,856
[Dongwoon Furniture]

924
00:58:19,856 --> 00:58:21,683
Twenty percent off for a set.

925
00:58:21,683 --> 00:58:24,395
Welcome. Can I help you find anything?

926
00:58:24,395 --> 00:58:25,923
I'm just looking around.

927
00:58:25,923 --> 00:58:27,890
Sure. Take your time.

928
00:58:28,690 --> 00:58:31,310
Just write your address here.

929
00:58:31,310 --> 00:58:34,590
We'll have it delivered by truck tomorrow.

930
00:58:34,590 --> 00:58:37,590
[Dongwoon Furniture, We Sell the Cheapest]

931
00:58:38,687 --> 00:58:40,390
I'm back.

932
00:58:45,191 --> 00:58:48,739
You left for that delivery ages ago.
Why are you only getting back now?

933
00:58:48,739 --> 00:58:50,655
Were you goofing off somewhere again?

934
00:58:50,655 --> 00:58:55,549
No. I took a wrong turn
on the way. I'm sorry.

935
00:58:55,549 --> 00:58:58,207
And what about the chair
delivered to Taeheung-dong this morning?

936
00:58:58,207 --> 00:59:02,741
What did you do this time?
We got a complaint saying one leg is wobbly.

937
00:59:02,741 --> 00:59:03,991
What?

938
00:59:03,991 --> 00:59:06,390
Well... that can't be right.

939
00:59:06,390 --> 00:59:10,399
How many times have I told you to be careful
when carrying things up and down?

940
00:59:10,399 --> 00:59:13,987
Why do you keep making us
go back for repairs? Oh, my.

941
00:59:13,987 --> 00:59:16,923
How am I supposed to keep you on like this?

942
00:59:16,923 --> 00:59:19,023
I'm sorry. I'll make sure
it doesn't happen again.

943
00:59:19,023 --> 00:59:21,675
Forget it! Go back to work.

944
00:59:21,675 --> 00:59:23,247
Jeez.

945
00:59:23,247 --> 00:59:25,023
I'm sorry.

946
00:59:25,672 --> 00:59:29,290
Jeez, that punk is really
on my case. Darn it.

947
00:59:36,256 --> 00:59:38,623
[Dongwoon Furniture]

948
00:59:51,359 --> 00:59:53,290
Darn it.

949
01:01:06,262 --> 01:01:08,762
Darn it! Seriously!

950
01:01:27,607 --> 01:01:29,307
Hey!

951
01:01:31,634 --> 01:01:33,334
You punk!

952
01:01:34,551 --> 01:01:36,256
Honey!

953
01:01:38,359 --> 01:01:42,111
So why did you keep ignoring me? Why?

954
01:01:42,111 --> 01:01:44,323
Why?

955
01:01:44,323 --> 01:01:46,023
You punk!

956
01:01:48,803 --> 01:01:51,890
Police! Drop the knife, Jang Eun Hak!

957
01:01:57,647 --> 01:01:58,923
Shoot me.

958
01:01:58,923 --> 01:02:01,621
Go ahead. Shoot me, you punk!

959
01:02:01,621 --> 01:02:04,623
If you want to see her die right here...

960
01:02:04,623 --> 01:02:08,823
Please help me...

961
01:02:12,623 --> 01:02:14,807
Last warning.

962
01:02:14,807 --> 01:02:16,155
Drop the knife, Jang Eun Hak.

963
01:02:16,155 --> 01:02:19,837
Who on earth are you to tell me
what to do, you punk?

964
01:02:19,837 --> 01:02:21,839
I'll decide what to do
with my own knife, you punk!

965
01:02:21,839 --> 01:02:22,847
Jang Eun Hak!

966
01:02:22,847 --> 01:02:26,383
Please help me.

967
01:02:26,383 --> 01:02:27,623
Help me.

968
01:02:27,623 --> 01:02:31,307
Please help me.

969
01:02:31,307 --> 01:02:33,295
Let the woman go.

970
01:02:33,295 --> 01:02:38,500
I'm going to kill every punk
who looks down on me!

971
01:02:38,500 --> 01:02:40,223
You little punks, huh?

972
01:02:40,223 --> 01:02:41,890
Hey, you looked down on me too, didn't you?

973
01:02:41,890 --> 01:02:43,590
You little...

974
01:02:50,390 --> 01:02:51,390
Drop the knife, Jang Eun Hak!

975
01:02:51,390 --> 01:02:53,523
Honey, honey!

976
01:03:00,223 --> 01:03:01,956
Jang Eun Hak!

977
01:03:04,755 --> 01:03:07,023
Apply pressure to stop the bleeding
and call an ambulance.

978
01:03:07,023 --> 01:03:08,723
Hurry!

979
01:03:20,279 --> 01:03:21,979
Hey!

980
01:03:36,235 --> 01:03:38,356
You punk, stop right there!

981
01:03:43,275 --> 01:03:44,990
Jang Eun Hak!

982
01:03:50,903 --> 01:03:52,603
Hey!

983
01:03:55,307 --> 01:03:57,007
Stop!

984
01:03:58,631 --> 01:04:01,023
Jang Eun Hak, stop!

985
01:04:01,823 --> 01:04:03,756
Jang Eun Hak, stop!

986
01:04:17,263 --> 01:04:18,963
Dong Jin!

987
01:05:19,695 --> 01:05:21,659
Dong Jin!

988
01:05:21,659 --> 01:05:24,756
What if you run into your husband?

989
01:05:24,756 --> 01:05:27,403
Tae Seong, what do I do?

990
01:05:27,403 --> 01:05:29,551
You should get out of there for now.

991
01:05:29,551 --> 01:05:32,956
The area was huge, so I'm not sure
we covered every route.

992
01:05:32,956 --> 01:05:35,556
So we don't know
where something could come from.

993
01:05:35,556 --> 01:05:37,190
Guess what I found?

994
01:05:37,190 --> 01:05:39,459
Mommy.

995
01:05:39,459 --> 01:05:42,839
Dong Jin, the law isn't perfect.
And you know that, right?

996
01:05:42,839 --> 01:05:44,619
I'll do my job,

997
01:05:44,619 --> 01:05:45,775
[Resignation Letter]
so you do yours.

998
01:05:45,775 --> 01:05:47,267
You're a reporter.

999
01:05:47,267 --> 01:05:49,123
[An Exclusive, Kingfisher...]
My husband has his work to do,

1000
01:05:49,123 --> 01:05:51,690
and I have mine...
